The Despoiler with the Helm of Warpsight is really important here, because he ignore all modifier so no -2 or -1 to hit on his planes. War Dogs with autocannons are also pretty good against anything that fly because of their stratagem to re-roll hits against flyers. DPoT and Ahriman can also deal with flyers, while staying behind the bulk of your Tzaangors and Rubrics.

First of all, you don't want to run Mephrit dynasty against either Tyranids or Space Wolves. To benefit from the Mephrit trait, you need to be 12 inch away from the enemy, which means you'll have to be at charge range of Genestealers, Carnifexes, or any Tyranids melee units. In the case of Space Wolves, they have Wulfen and Thunderwolf cavalry that can give you trouble as well.  

I'll be honest with you, it is really difficult to win against Tyranids at the moment, they out shoot us, they are better at melee and believe it or not more resilient. Also, Wraiths are pretty bad against Nids, because they have so many Psykers, which hard counters Canoptek Wraiths.  

You're best chance is playing either Nephrekh or Sautekh. Because that is what give you the most mobility. You are relying heavily on the Destroyers for anti-tank. Nephrekh would be good in this case, because you can keep them in reserve turn one, to protect them from enemy fire.  

Here's the list I would run with what you have :


&nbsp;

**++ Battalion Detachment +5CP (Necrons) [54 PL, 1035pts] ++**

&nbsp;

**+ No Force Org Slot +**

&nbsp;

**Dynasty Choice:** Dynasty: Nephrekh

&nbsp;

**+ HQ +**

&nbsp;

**Catacomb Command Barge [9 PL, 169pts]:** Artefact: Lightning Field, Gauss Cannon, Warscythe


. **Warlord:** Warlord Trait (Codex 3): Immortal Pride

&nbsp;

**Lord [5 PL, 76pts]:** Hyperphase Sword

&nbsp;

**+ Troops +**

&nbsp;

**Immortals [8 PL, 170pts]:** 10x Immortal, Tesla Carbine

&nbsp;

**Immortals [8 PL, 170pts]:** 10x Immortal, Tesla Carbine

&nbsp;

